Caption:\
\uc0\u55358 \u56800  RAG isn't just a Vector Database + LLM.\
\
A production-ready Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system is an entire pipeline.\
\
It starts with data ingestion, chunking, embeddings, and vector storage. When a user asks a question, the system retrieves the most relevant context using semantic or hybrid search, re-ranks the results, constructs an optimized prompt, and finally lets the LLM generate an accurate, context-aware response.\
\
When built correctly, RAG helps:\
\'95 Reduce hallucinations\
\'95 Keep answers grounded in your own data\
\'95 Deliver up-to-date information\
\'95 Build reliable enterprise AI applications\
\
Whether you're building AI copilots, internal knowledge bases, customer support assistants, or intelligent search systems, understanding the complete RAG architecture is essential.\
\
At OneView, we're passionate about building modern AI-powered applications that solve real-world problems.\
